@startuml
!include _style.iuml
title Library Management System: Borrow and Return Activity Diagram

|Member|
start
:Search for a book;
:View details and availability;
if (Copies available?) then (no: all copies on loan)
  :Reserve the book;
  |System|
  if (Member eligible to reserve?\n(account active, no unpaid fines)) then (yes)
    :Add member to reservation queue;
    :Send queue confirmation;
    |Member|
    :Receive confirmation;
    stop
  else (no)
    |System|
    :Reject reservation with reason;
    |Member|
    :Receive rejection notice;
    stop
  endif
else (yes)
  :Submit borrow request;
endif
|System|
if (Member eligible?\n(account active, no unpaid fines,\nactive loans + pending requests < 3)) then (yes)
  |Librarian|
  :Review borrow request;
  if (Confirm request?) then (yes)
    |System|
    :Re-check member and copy;
    if (Still eligible and copy available?) then (yes)
      :Record loan (borrow date, due date = +14 days);
      :Mark copy as On Loan;
      |Member|
      :Receive loan confirmation (due date);
    else (no)
      |System|
      :Reject request with reason;
      |Member|
      :Receive rejection notice;
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    |System|
    :Reject request with reason;
    |Member|
    :Receive rejection notice;
    stop
  endif
else (no)
  |System|
  :Reject request with reason;
  |Member|
  :Receive rejection notice;
  stop
endif
|Member|
:Borrow and read the book;
:Initiate return;
|Librarian|
:Process returned book;
|System|
if (Returned after due date?) then (yes)
  :Calculate fine\n(5 EGP x overdue days);
  :Add fine to member account\n(stays unpaid until paid);
else (no)
endif
if (Reservation queue waiting?) then (yes)
  :Mark copy as Reserved;
  :Notify next member in queue;
  |Member|
  :Receive availability notice;
else (no)
  |System|
  :Mark copy as Available;
endif
stop

note right
  Fine payment is a separate step (not part of the return):
  the librarian records the payment when the member pays
  at the desk. The unpaid-fine block is lifted then.
  FR-16 overdue loans are also listed in the overdue report
  by the system; fines are created at return.
end note
@enduml
